  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Hello VRChat Support,\n\nI’m reaching out to report an issue I’ve been experiencing in VRChat after the most recent update. Specifically, when I use any avatar, the hands are severely misaligned, with all of my fingers appearing bent backwards. This issue makes it very difficult to engage in gameplay or use any in-game gestures. Here are the details of my setup:\n\nHeadset: Pimax 5K Super (running SteamVR)\n\nControllers: Valve Index controllers\n\nCPU: AMD 9700X\n\nGPU: NVIDIA RTX 4080\n\nRAM: 96GB DDR5\n\nStorage: 4TB M.2\n\nThe hand tracking issue affects all avatars, and I’ve tested several to rule out the possibility of an avatar-specific problem. The fingers consistently appear bent backward in-game, and the controller tracking seems misaligned and out of sync. This issue is unique to VRChat, as I have not encountered similar problems in other VR applications or games.\n\nAdditionally, I’ve noticed minor tracking issues that began after the release of the latest Pimax Play tool, which might be contributing to the problem.\n\nI would appreciate any troubleshooting steps or assistance you can provide to resolve this issue.\n\nThank you for your time and support.",
